                                        {
                                            "type": "table",
                                            "html": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"4\"><p><strong>IEC 60601-1-6</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Clause</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Requirement + Test</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Compliance method </strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Result</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a></a><strong>4.0</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>General requirements</strong></p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4.1</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>Conditions for application to ME EQUIPMENT</strong></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>The ME EQUIPMENT shall provide adequate USABLITY such that the RISks resulting from</p><p>NORMAL USE, i.e. CORRECT USE and USE ERROR ,are acceptable.</p></td><td><p>Compliance with 4.2 and other clauses and subclauses of this collateral standard</p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4.2</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>USABILITY ENGINEERING PROCESS for ME EQUIPMENT</strong></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>A USABILITY ENGINEERING PROCESS complying with IEC 62366-1:2015+A1:2020 shall be performed except:</p><p>- the planning for and execution of production and POST-PRODUCTION monitoring in thecontext of applying the USABILITY ENGINEERING PROCESS within the framework ofISO 14971，and</p><p>- maintenance of the USABILITY ENGINEERING PROCESS</p></td><td><p>USABILITY ENGINEERING PROCESS has been performed, please see the inspection of the USABILITY ENGINEERING file</p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>5</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>ME EQUIPMENT ACCOMPANYING DOCUMENTS</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>P</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>The instructions for use include a brief description of the me equipment, its physical operating principles and significant physical and performance characteristics relevant to its use. </p></td><td><p>Inspect the instruction for use to include information required</p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>The same information shall also be included in the technical description, if this is provided as a separate document.</p></td><td><p>Inspect the instruction for use to include information required</p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>The instructions for use contain a summary of the USE SPECIFICATION as specified in IEC 62366-1:2015+A1:2020, 5.1.</p></td><td><p>Inspect the instruction for use to include  use specification as specifed in IEC 62366-1.</p></td><td><p>P</p></td></tr></table>"
